## Original Apple Log numerical reference

The PIPE implementation and its numerical tests use the published original
Apple Log definitions and constants. The reference used was
[ACES `CSC.Apple.AppleLog_to_ACES.ctl`](https://github.com/aces-aswf/aces-input-and-colorspaces/blob/2331f7d915c13ae99a5c203393bace972816c413/apple/CSC.Apple.AppleLog_to_ACES.ctl),
revision `2331f7d915c13ae99a5c203393bace972816c413`, file SHA-256
`0517071538c5ce19282773acf3f3a6b54f932ac3137eb28aae14db890cdc0feb`.

The `apple_inverse_reference` test helper in
`crates/mcraw4vulkan-render/tests/direct_yuv12_contract.rs` follows the
reference's `AppleLog_to_linear` routine. Its local adaptation uses Rust f64,
inlined constants, reordered branches and `exp2`, without the ACES gamut
conversion. Attribution for the reference-derived inverse is retained here
and beside that helper:

    SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
    Copyright Contributors to the ACES Project.

The reference-derived material retains its Apache-2.0 terms. A complete copy
of the [Apache License, Version 2.0](licenses/gl_generator-0.14.0-LICENSE-Apache-2_0-33bdcf7e06-cfc7749b96f6.txt)
is included in the existing legal payload; this is the same license text used
by the [pinned ACES reference](https://github.com/aces-aswf/aces-input-and-colorspaces/blob/2331f7d915c13ae99a5c203393bace972816c413/LICENSE).
The remaining mcraw4vulkan-owned source retains the GPL terms stated above.
No CTL interpreter or ACES gamut conversion is required by PIPE; the upstream
CTL file is not bundled with the application or its public source export.
